## Scope
The KPI Standardization tooling at `/admin/kpi-standardization` (7 tabs) governs canonical KPI naming via `kpi_definitions` + `kpi_name_aliases`. Forward-only: pre-May-2026 KPI rows are FROZEN and never modified.

## Key contracts
- **Idempotent approval.** `useBuildRegistry.createDefinitionWithAliases` MUST look up an existing definition by `(canonical_kra_name, canonical_kpi_name)` before inserting, and only insert aliases not already linked. Race on `23505` falls back to re-read.
- **Inline canonical edit (Build Registry).** Admins can override the canonical KRA/KPI text before approval. Empty/whitespace blocks submission.
- **Edit canonical (Review Registry).** `useEditDefinition` updates `kpi_definitions` text. *Propagate* mode also runs `correct_may_kpis` for every May-2026+ `(period, year)` tuple currently linked.
- **`correct_may_kpis` (DB)** rejects pre-May-2026 dates and now records full before-image (affected `kpi.id`s + prior `kpi_definition_id`) into `kpi_standardization_actions` so undo can revert each row exactly.

## Reversibility (Phase 5b — §88I)
- Single append-only `kpi_standardization_actions` table; admin SELECT/INSERT only, no UPDATE/DELETE policy.
- `reverse_standardization_action(uuid)` is the only undo path. Refuses already-reversed rows. For `create_definition`, refuses when any `kpis.kpi_definition_id` still references the definition.
- Reversed rows stay in the History tab (dimmed) — never hidden. Confirmation goes through `ConfirmDestructiveDialog`.

## Drill-in
`AffectedKpisTable` is the shared paginated (25/page) read-only viewer. Used in Build Registry (per variant), Review Registry (per definition), and Correct May KPIs (per signature). Reads from `kpis` joined to `profiles` for employee names. NEVER exposes write actions.

## Scanner invariant (May 2026)
- `scan_kpi_duplicate_groups` MUST emit exactly one variant entry per distinct `(category_id, kra_name, kpi_name)`. The historical bug joined `kpis` back to its own aggregate and inflated `variants` by `row_count`.
- Client-side `dedupeScannerGroups` (in `src/lib/scanGroupsDedup.ts`) is a defence-in-depth pass: even if a stale function returns duplicates, `useScanDuplicates` collapses them before render. Tests in `src/lib/scanGroupsDedup.test.ts` lock the behaviour.
- **Alias-aware exclusion:** a variant that already exists in `kpi_name_aliases` (matched by `category_id` + case-insensitive `kra_name` + `kpi_name`) is filtered out. After the filter, a group with <2 distinct KRA names is dropped. This means **approved groups never reappear on Re-scan** without depending on `kpis.kpi_definition_id` being backfilled.
- **Grouped-column rule:** the inner `sub` CTE precomputes `norm_kpi = LOWER(TRIM(kpi_name))` so the outer aggregate's correlated `EXISTS` against `kpi_scanner_skips` only references grouped columns (`s.cat_id`, `s.norm_kpi`). Referencing the raw `s.kpi_name` inside the subquery breaks Postgres ("subquery uses ungrouped column"). Any future edit to the scanner must keep this invariant.

## Persistent "Don't Merge" skips
- Admin-only `kpi_scanner_skips` table keyed on `(category_id, normalized_kpi)`, no UPDATE policy.
- `scan_kpi_duplicate_groups(p_include_skipped boolean DEFAULT false)` hides skipped groups by default; with `true` it returns them tagged `is_skipped: true` so the UI dims them and offers **Restore (un-skip)**.
- Skip / un-skip log into `kpi_standardization_actions` (`skip_group` / `unskip_group`) and are reversible via the History tab — `reverse_standardization_action` removes / re-inserts the skip row. Confirmation goes through `ConfirmDestructiveDialog`.
- Hook: `useScannerSkips` (`skipGroup`, `unskipGroup`). UI: Build Registry tab adds **Don't merge** button + **Include skipped** toggle; HistoryUndoTab labels `skip_group` / `unskip_group`.

## Fuzzy scanner (May 2026)
- `scan_kpi_duplicate_groups(p_include_skipped boolean, p_fuzzy_threshold numeric DEFAULT 0.55)` uses `pg_trgm` similarity to cluster near-identical KPI names within the same category. The non-recursive LATERAL pass picks the lexicographically-smallest neighbour above threshold as the cluster representative — bounded O(N²) per category, kept fast by a `gin_trgm_ops` index on `LOWER(TRIM(kpi_name))`.
- Each variant is tagged `match_type: 'exact' | 'fuzzy'` plus a `similarity` score (0..1). Group-level `has_fuzzy` flags clusters that contain at least one fuzzy match.
- A group is emitted when **either** ≥2 distinct KRAs share the same KPI name (legacy rule) **or** ≥2 fuzzy-similar variants cluster together. This is what surfaces same-KPI/single-KRA leftovers like the "Fugitive Particulate Matter (PM10)" vs "(PM10/AQI)" pair after the user has approved the canonical.
- Skip-list keying is unchanged: `(category_id, normalized_kpi_of_representative)`. Loosening the threshold may surface a fuzzy cousin under a new representative — that is expected and admins can `Don't merge` it independently.
- UI: `BuildRegistryTab` exposes a **Match sensitivity** select (Strict 0.75 / Balanced 0.55 / Loose 0.40), badges every variant Exact / Fuzzy XX%, and defaults the canonical selection on fuzzy groups to the **longest** (most descriptive) variant. The **Don't merge** button per group remains the cleanup escape hatch.

## Out of scope
- Pre-May-2026 data is frozen everywhere. Even propagation skips it client-side; DB function rejects it anyway.
- The Registry Browser at `/registry` and `get_public_registry_view` remain read-only and never expose per-employee data.

## Phase 5c — Edit-always-propagates + retroactive link backfill (May 2026)
- `useEditDefinition` ALWAYS rewrites May-2026+ linked rows' `kra_name`/`kpi_name` columns. The `propagate` argument is kept for API compatibility but is not user-tunable; `EditDefinitionDialog` no longer shows the registry-only / propagate radio.
- `KpiHeaderSection` (the "View KPI Details" panel header) prefers `canonicalPair(variantPairs)` over the literal row text. This guarantees admin renames surface immediately on the user dashboard even before propagation finishes or for rows whose text columns lag.
- A one-shot SQL migration retroactively sets `kpis.kpi_definition_id` for May-2026+ rows whose `(category_id, kra_name, kpi_name)` matches a canonical or alias pair. Pre-May-2026 rows are excluded. Logged in `kpi_standardization_actions` as `backfill_definition_links` (new allowed action_type, append-only).
- The `kpi_standardization_actions_action_type_check` constraint now also allows `skip_group`, `unskip_group`, and `backfill_definition_links` (the first two were already produced by `useScannerSkips` but had been missing from the constraint).

## Canonical-aware consumers (cross-period UI)
Any UI that aggregates a single KPI across periods MUST resolve sibling rows via canonical definition + aliases — strict `kpi_name`/`kra_name` equality silently drops alias-renamed historical months. Use the shared helper `src/lib/canonicalRelatedKpis.ts`:
- `useCanonicalVariantPairs(kpi)` → React Query hook returning `[{kra_name, kpi_name}, …]` (canonical first, then aliases). Empty array when KPI is unregistered.
- `matchesCanonicalKpi(row, current, variantPairs)` → predicate. Falls back to strict equality when `variantPairs` is empty (legacy data).
- `preferredVariantRow(rows, variantPairs, currentKpiId)` → period-dedup tiebreaker (canonical → current id → first).

Current consumers: `src/components/review/KpiHistoryCard.tsx`, `src/components/dashboard/KpiTrackerModal.tsx`, `src/components/review/KpiJourneySection.tsx` (the latter still uses an inlined version of the resolver query for the prev-month batch fetch — keep its logic in lock-step). When adding new monthly/annual aggregation widgets, wire them through this helper instead of reimplementing the matcher.

## Group splitting (multi-canonical approval, May 2026)
A fuzzy cluster can contain semantically distinct KPIs (e.g. `Total Recordable Injury (LTI)` vs `(STI)`). The Build Registry UI lets admins **partition** any group into multiple buckets (`A`, `B`, `C`, …) plus a `Skip` bucket and approve all buckets in one click — each active bucket creates its own `kpi_definition` and links only its own variants as aliases.
- Helper: `src/lib/scanGroupBuckets.ts` (`summarizeBuckets`, `defaultCanonicalForBucket`, `nextAvailableBucket`, `suggestBucketAssignments`, `validateBuckets`). Tests in `scanGroupBuckets.test.ts` lock the contract.
- Hook: `useBuildRegistry.createMultipleDefinitionsWithAliases` loops the existing idempotent single-bucket call inside one saving lock, suppresses per-bucket toasts when ≥2 buckets are submitted, and emits one summary toast. The single-bucket path is unchanged.
- Default behaviour is identical to pre-split UX: every variant lives in bucket `A`, so the Approve button creates a single canonical exactly as before.
- `Suggest split` uses keyword heuristics (LTI → A, STI → B, PM10 → A, PM10/AQI → B, PM2.5 → B) to pre-assign buckets; the admin can override any cell.
- Variants assigned to `Skip` are excluded from approval and remain available for the next scan or for `Don't merge`.
- No DB changes. Re-running a partitioned approval is a no-op thanks to the idempotent definition + alias inserts.
